BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goldcoast-17v76cj@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260908T130000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260908T150000
SUMMARY:Lunch Law Talks: Bail Laws
DESCRIPTION:Bail is a fundamental part of Australia's criminal justice syst
 em\, based on the principle that a person is presumed innocent until prove
 n guilty. Under the Bail Act 2013 (NSW) \, courts must determine whether a
 n accused person poses an unacceptable risk of failing to appear in court\
 , committing further offences\, endangering others\, or interfering with t
 he administration of justice. Bail decisions therefore require a careful b
 alance between protecting the rights of the accused and ensuring community
  safety. Recent high-profile domestic violence and youth crime cases have 
 intensified public debate about whether that balance is being achieved.
LOCATION:Southern Cross University Gold Coast
URL:https://www.scu.edu.au/business-law-and-arts/events/lunch-law-talks-sep
 tember/
END:VEVENT
