BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goldcoast-1qa7nd1@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260910T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260910T210000
SUMMARY:Dear Seattle Regional Aus Tour 2026
DESCRIPTION:Sydney punk rockers Dear Seattle are hitting the road this Augu
 st\, announcing an extensive regional Australian headline tour with very s
 pecial guests Seahaven (US) who will be making their debut visit to our sh
 ores\, and Bad Neighbour. Tickets are on sale now via Destroy All Lines Wi
 th a distinctive Aussie tinge to their emotive and propulsive wares\, Dear
  Seattle are a headbanging-with-heart punk rock band from Sydney’s North
 ern Beaches. One part mosh pit\, and one part love letter\, the band have 
 created a truly unique and powerful style of songwriting that’s connecti
 ng with fans across Australia and the rest of the world. Whether charming 
 Missy Higgins herself with their 2019 triple j Like A Version of "The Spec
 ial Two"\, launching their own beer\, burning up the charts and airwaves\,
  or penning melodic\, sing along anthems\, Dear Seattle are a band who bui
 ld unforgettable moments with charming execution. Their latest album\, TOY
  (Domestic La La)\, released last year and marked a major milestone for th
 e band\, debuting at #4 on the ARIA Albums Chart and earning Dear Seattle 
 their first ever Top 10 ARIA chart position. Following a massive year of s
 hows all over the world\, TOY was re-released earlier this year as an expa
 nded edition featuring two bonus tracks. Joining Dear Seattle on their tre
 k across Australia is Seahaven\, an alternative rock band from Torrance\, 
 California\, known for blending emotionally raw songwriting with melodic\,
  atmospheric guitar-driven music. Over nearly two decades\, the band has e
 arned a devoted following through acclaimed releases including Winter Fore
 ver\, Reverie Lagoon: Music for Escapism Only\, Halo of Hurt\, and their s
 elf-titled 2026 album. With introspective lyrics\, dynamic arrangements\, 
 and a sound that balances melancholy with soaring hooks\, Seahaven continu
 es to evolve while staying true to the honesty that has defined the band f
 rom the beginning. With special guests Seahaven (USA)\, Bad Neighbour and 
 Wifecult. WILL SELL OUT / GET IN EARLY! Doors at 7pm. El Ranchero back dec
 k/bar and Spanish Girl Food Co will be open from 6pm for preshow dinner an
 d drinks. DEAR SEATTLE Mo's Desert Clubhouse (GOLD COAST) Thursday 10 Sept
 ember 2026 // 7pm doors Tickets $59.90 inc BF // 18+ Mo's is Burleigh Head
 s' most loved music venue\, licensed bars\, creative studios and cultural 
 hub. The Warehouse & El Ranchero both boast epic bar menus\, cocktails and
  craft beers. Mo's is a fully licensed venue\, all guests are required to 
 show ID on entry. Tickets will only be refunded through event cancellation
  or production of a medical certificate within 24hrs of show doors.
LOCATION:Mo's Desert Clubhouse
URL:https://tickets.oztix.com.au/outlet/event/f5c99a80-f2bc-45b0-affb-739a3
 06389c9
END:VEVENT
